ed for Laravel Cashier\nbefore, Vatly will feel immediately familiar — a ",[432,433,434],"code",{},"Billable"," trait, ",[432,437,438],{},"subscribed()",",\n",[432,441,442],{},"subscription()->swap()",", a wired-up webhook endpoint. The difference is what sits ",[445,446,447],"em",{},"behind","\nthe API: Vatly is a ",[450,451,452],"strong",{},"Merchant of Record",", so it is the legal seller and handles VAT,\ninvoicing, and payment compliance for you — and it's ",[450,455,456],{},"Europe-first",", operating under EU\njurisdiction.",[428,459,460,461,464,465,439,472,477,478,483],{},"This page is an honest, side-by-side look at how ",[432,462,463],{},"vatly-laravel"," stacks up against the\nCashier-style packages you might otherwise reach for —\n",[466,467,471],"a",{"href":468,"rel":469},"https:\u002F\u002Flaravel.com\u002Fdocs\u002F12.x\u002Fbilling",[470],"nofollow","Laravel Cashier (Stripe)",[466,473,476],{"href":474,"rel":475},"https:\u002F\u002Flaravel.com\u002Fdocs\u002F12.x\u002Fcashier-paddle",[470],"Laravel Cashier (Paddle)",", and\n",[466,479,482],{"href":480,"rel":481},"https:\u002F\u002Fgithub.com\u002Flmsqueezy\u002Flaravel",[470],"Lemon Squeezy for Laravel"," — gaps included.",[485,486,487,490,491,493],"note",{},[450,488,489],{},"Already running one of these in an existing app?"," This page helps you choose. Once you\nhave, ",[466,492,208],{"href":209}," shows how to add Vatly\nnext to your current biller and migrate customers over gradually.",[495,496],"hr",{},[498,499,501],"h2",{"id":500},"at-a-glance","At a glance",[503,504,505,528],"table",{},[506,507,508],"thead",{},[509,510,511,514,517,520,523],"tr",{},[512,513],"th",{},[512,515,516],{},"Cashier (Stripe Billing)",[512,518,519],{},"Cashier (Paddle)",[512,521,522],{},"Lemon Squeezy",[512,524,525],{},[450,526,527],{},"Vatly",[529,530,531,557,582,602,631,654,691,715,740,757,773,791],"tbody",{},[509,532,533,537,542,547,552],{},[534,535,536],"td",{},"Composer package",[534,538,539],{},[432,540,541],{},"la